cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "civgrad: a differentiable, hierarchical Petri net of the global supply chain"
authors:
  - family-names: Wallar
    given-names: Alex
repository-code: "https://github.com/a20r/civgrad"
url: "https://a20r.github.io/civgrad/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-22"
keywords:
  - supply chains
  - resilience
  - Petri nets
  - differentiable simulation
  - JAX
abstract: >-
  A differentiable, hierarchical Petri net of the global supply chain:
  discrete structural analyses (single points of failure, deadlock and
  livelock detection), a JAX fluid relaxation with capacity/stockpile
  gradients over a disruption prior, an adaptation law that makes recovery
  time emergent, and a frozen historical-replay validation protocol whose
  public scorecard shows its misses as prominently as its hits.
